About

    A merge of my dice_restart patch and the oagertz/dice patch.


Usage (*)
(*) See e.g. patch/tepper/namelist/h_00_gh0_lr_ofe_wh_rs.nml

    &RESTART_PARAMS
    nrestart2=N        ! restart at snapshot N
    add_dice_ic=.true. ! optional, to load additional DICE ICs at restart (**)
    restart_vars=6,7   	!-> corresponds to the actual indices of passive scalars (excluding temperature)
    /

    &INIT_PARAMS
    filetype='ramses_dice'
    /

    &RUN_PARAMS
    nrestart=0
    /


    (**) If add_dice_ic=.true., then the file(s) pointed at by
        &DICE_PARAMS
        ic_file='some_ics.g2'
        ic_nfile=N
        /
    will be loaded. Also, may need to set some other DICE relevant parameters, but beware that the following are set by default to (for good reason):
        IG_rho=0.0D0                 ! IGM gas density (default 1.0d-5)
        IG_T2=0.0D0                  ! IGM gas temperature (default: 1.0d7)
        IG_metal=0.0                 ! IGM metallicity (solar units)


Notes
    N/A


To-Do

    - Remove obsolete bits such as uu for particles, etc.


Bugs (see also patch/tepper/dice_restart/README)

    - stellar masses go below 0 when simulation time is correctly read at restart (see init_part.f90, around lines 2717-22); the fix is to set t=0 at restart, but this affects the stellar ages and thus their subsequent evolution (see feedback.f90, around line 475, look for 'Age at t')
    -> Perhaps related to the issue with 'Main step' and 'nstep_coarse'.
    -> Perhaps related to MISSING patched init_time.f90 (see restart patch)

    - mcons and econs are reset to 0; bug or not?

    - Main step starts at 1 instead of at the actual last value at restart; the same is true for nstep_coarse
    -> Perhaps related to the issue with stellar ages.

    - When loading additional DICE ICs, there may be a potential issue with duplicate particle ids (iord)

    - Some particles end up at or beyond the box boundary at restart
    The fix for now is to toss these, which is not fully consistent with the restart snapshot state


Modifications
** Note that not all modifications are detailed as they are, but they can be easily searched for with the information provided

    init_part.90:
    Copy over file from oagertz/dice/ and merge with file in oagertz/bck_29JUL2025/dice_restart/
